# oracle: pair_style extep (BN.extep, elements B N) on the 100-atom BN sample of examples/PACKAGES/extep (in.extep-bn), NVE instead of the example's NPT, 50 steps, 300 K velocities as the example.
# native: b332f28 (installed /home/roy/.local/bin/lmp)
# measured 2026-10-14 (engine vs native, max relative error, thermo |a-b|/|b|, per-atom |a-b|/max(1,|b|)): thermo 2.9e-13, per-atom 1.1e-13; passes at rel 1e-8 abs 1e-10.
# oracle-inputs: w145pr_BN.data
# w145pr_BN.data is a byte copy of examples/PACKAGES/extep/BN.data (the example data file)
# oracle-potentials: BN.extep
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           metal
boundary        p p p
atom_style      atomic
processors      * * 1
read_data       w145pr_BN.data
pair_style      extep
pair_coeff      * * BN.extep B N
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
timestep        0.0001
velocity        all create 300.0 12345
fix             1 all nve
thermo_style    custom step time etotal pe temp lx ly lz pxx pyy pzz
thermo_modify   format float %.15g norm no
thermo          10
run             50
